WEBVTT

00:01.001 --> 00:03.920
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:32.592 --> 01:34.177
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:34.260 --> 01:35.428
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:44.521 --> 01:46.397
Starting today, this will be your room.

01:47.357 --> 01:48.900
A storage shed...?

01:49.484 --> 01:51.861
You're seriously telling me to live here?

01:51.945 --> 01:54.239
Yes. Reflect on your actions.

01:57.492 --> 02:00.161
Lady Yinghua, are you alright?

02:03.373 --> 02:04.999
Of course not!

02:05.083 --> 02:07.752
Collecting all that junk!
You're unbelievable.

02:08.336 --> 02:10.630
At this rate, Lady Hongniang
will kick you out of your room

02:10.713 --> 02:12.507
and you'll be banished
to the storage shed!

02:14.467 --> 02:15.677
That sounds great.

02:17.262 --> 02:20.014
The storage shed is bigger than
my current room.

02:20.098 --> 02:22.267
And even if I make noise at night...

02:22.350 --> 02:24.936
- Maomao?
- Not bad.

02:25.520 --> 02:27.564
Now that it's decided, let's hurry.

02:27.647 --> 02:29.983
I need to get back quickly
and ask Lady Hongniang about this.

02:30.066 --> 02:33.528
Wait. Hey... wait!

02:40.869 --> 02:41.744
What is all this...?

02:44.455 --> 02:46.583
Make sure you reflect properly.

02:46.666 --> 02:48.042
Lady Hongniang...

02:48.126 --> 02:50.253
Thank you so much!

02:50.837 --> 02:53.756
I'll dry medicinal herbs here!
And I'll prepare medicines here!

02:53.840 --> 02:56.175
This goes there, and that goes here...!

02:57.635 --> 03:00.805
See? I told you it’s pointless!

03:01.556 --> 03:04.559
The storage shed? Unbelievable.

03:05.310 --> 03:07.770
Isn't telling Lady Hongniang

03:07.854 --> 03:10.189
a bit too much, Yinghua?

03:10.857 --> 03:12.483
It wasn’t me!

03:12.567 --> 03:15.820
Maomao asked Lady Hongniang herself.

03:15.904 --> 03:17.363
Right, Maomao?

03:17.447 --> 03:19.949
Yes. It was quite convenient for me
in many ways.

03:20.033 --> 03:21.451
What?

03:22.619 --> 03:23.870
That aside,

03:23.953 --> 03:27.123
Maomao, you need to stop
collecting bugs, okay?

03:27.206 --> 03:28.374
Bugs?

03:28.458 --> 03:31.669
Actually, I'm collecting lizard tails...

03:32.253 --> 03:35.673
And besides, I haven't collected any
since Lady Yinghua collapsed.

03:35.757 --> 03:37.884
Really?

03:37.967 --> 03:41.763
But there's a rumor going around that
a strange court lady is catching bugs

03:41.846 --> 03:43.139
while laughing.

03:43.723 --> 03:45.808
I've done no such thing.

03:45.892 --> 03:48.311
<i>I did collect moths for a job,</i>

03:48.394 --> 03:50.313
<i>but I never laughed while catching bugs...</i>

03:55.944 --> 03:58.112
<i>This is a serious matter.</i>

03:59.030 --> 04:02.116
Huh? Did I see Shisui lately?

04:02.825 --> 04:06.079
Yeah. Have you seen Shisui around lately?

04:06.663 --> 04:08.289
Shisui, huh?

04:08.373 --> 04:11.459
That girl is always vanishing
and reappearing out of nowhere.

04:14.671 --> 04:18.341
Hey, hey! Does anyone know
where Shisui is?

04:18.424 --> 04:19.926
Shisui?

04:20.009 --> 04:22.387
I might've seen her... or maybe not.

04:22.470 --> 04:25.765
Huh? Where did you see her? Tell me!

04:25.848 --> 04:28.184
Well...

04:29.978 --> 04:33.898
<i>Is she wary because
I'm the attendant assigned to the consort?</i>

04:35.400 --> 04:36.567
<i>Someone like Xiaolan,</i>

04:36.651 --> 04:40.488
<i>who treats everyone equally,
is actually pretty rare.</i>

04:41.239 --> 04:43.366
<i>Maybe I can bait them with something.</i>

04:44.367 --> 04:45.243
<i>Oh, this might work...</i>

04:45.952 --> 04:48.037
Depending on
how detailed your information is,

04:48.621 --> 04:50.540
I might just give this to you.

04:51.374 --> 04:53.459
Use it. You're bleeding.

04:57.672 --> 04:58.881
This is...

04:58.965 --> 05:01.342
Could it possibly belong to that person?

05:02.093 --> 05:03.845
I'll leave it to your imagination.

05:04.887 --> 05:07.473
Now, would you mind
telling me her whereabouts?

05:11.686 --> 05:13.187
<i>From what they told me,</i>

05:13.271 --> 05:16.607
<i>she's often seen in the northern thicket...</i>

05:16.691 --> 05:19.235
<i>Come to think of it,
I ran into her around here before.</i>

05:19.319 --> 05:21.529
<i>Perhaps this is her favorite spot.</i>

05:27.452 --> 05:30.330
I should've brought some
mosquito repellent.

05:31.664 --> 05:32.832
Marvel-of-Peru...

05:33.583 --> 05:35.418
So they were growing here.

05:37.420 --> 05:39.881
<i>I remember when I was little,
I used to go pick their seeds</i>

05:39.964 --> 05:42.633
<i>with the courtesans.</i>

05:43.301 --> 05:46.137
<i>However the powder inside wasn't used
as face powder,</i>

05:46.804 --> 05:49.057
<i>but to make an abortion pill.</i>

05:51.517 --> 05:54.187
<i>Shin originally didn't wear perfume.</i>

05:55.188 --> 05:58.524
<i>Shin, who was trying to replace
Lady Lihua as a consort,</i>

05:58.608 --> 06:02.403
<i>avoiding a pregnancy risk is not strange.</i>

06:02.904 --> 06:03.863
<i>But despite that,</i>

06:03.946 --> 06:07.158
<i>Shin deliberately wore perfume
while trying to make an abortion pill.</i>

06:07.241 --> 06:08.743
<i>Which means...</i>

06:09.577 --> 06:11.329
<i>It's not as if only Lady Gyokuyou</i>

06:11.412 --> 06:14.457
<i>receives the Emperor's favor.</i>

06:14.540 --> 06:18.252
<i>It's entirely possible that
Lady Lihua is pregnant as well.</i>

06:19.462 --> 06:23.257
<i>But the strange part about
that incident isn't just that.</i>

06:23.966 --> 06:28.096
<i>The abortion pill made by the courtesans,
aside from Marvel-of-Peru flowers,</i>

06:28.179 --> 06:31.516
<i>can also be made with
Chinese lantern plants, peonies, balsam,</i>

06:31.599 --> 06:33.142
<i>as well as quicksilver.</i>

06:33.893 --> 06:34.852
<i>Leaving quicksilver aside,</i>

06:34.936 --> 06:37.980
<i>the rest are flowers that can be
obtained within the rear palace.</i>

06:38.689 --> 06:40.483
<i>And yet,</i>

06:40.566 --> 06:41.984
<i>Shin sourced the ingredients
for the abortion pill</i>

06:42.068 --> 06:45.154
<i>from supplies brought in by the caravan.</i>

06:45.238 --> 06:48.449
<i>In other words,
someone must have taught Shin,</i>

06:48.533 --> 06:51.536
<i>who had no knowledge of medicine,
how to make poison.</i>

06:52.120 --> 06:55.498
<i>And that person is likely
still within the rear palace...</i>

07:00.378 --> 07:02.964
Gotcha!

07:03.047 --> 07:06.175
Wait, wait, wait!

07:06.259 --> 07:08.761
<i>Being lumped together
with someone like that...</i>

07:08.845 --> 07:09.804
<i>That's just insulting.</i>

07:09.887 --> 07:11.931
Gotcha!

07:20.940 --> 07:21.941
A bug!

07:25.153 --> 07:26.404
Shisui...

07:26.487 --> 07:28.948
I’d appreciate it
if you could move your hands.

07:33.369 --> 07:36.539
- Sorry, Maomao.
- Whatever.

07:37.123 --> 07:40.418
- Were you trying to catch those bugs?
- Yes.

07:41.002 --> 07:43.129
<i>She must really like bugs.</i>

07:51.053 --> 07:54.390
This bug lives on
an island nation in the East,

07:54.474 --> 07:56.142
and it makes sounds
by rubbing its wings together.

07:56.225 --> 07:59.353
It probably escaped
from some traded goods.

07:59.437 --> 08:00.938
Like that moth I caught before,

08:01.022 --> 08:02.857
it likely only exists here.

08:02.940 --> 08:04.692
It kind of looks like a cockroach,

08:04.775 --> 08:06.402
but it’s different, so don’t worry.

08:06.486 --> 08:08.321
And you know,
I have so much more to tell you!

08:08.404 --> 08:10.031
<i>I shouldn't have asked.</i>

08:14.911 --> 08:16.412
<i>What’s that sound?</i>

08:25.713 --> 08:28.341
<i>That’s the Empress Dowager, isn’t it?</i>

08:29.008 --> 08:32.803
<i>I saw her at last year’s garden party,
but she looks so young.</i>

08:33.804 --> 08:36.390
<i>Hard to believe she’s
the Emperor’s mother.</i>

08:37.892 --> 08:39.352
Why are you hiding?

08:39.435 --> 08:40.853
You are too, Maomao.

08:42.104 --> 08:43.606
A reflex, I guess...

08:44.357 --> 08:46.192
Is she going to the clinic?

08:46.692 --> 08:48.528
- The clinic?
- Yeah.

08:48.611 --> 08:51.656
It's an unofficial clinic
run by the court ladies.

08:51.739 --> 08:53.407
I know about that.

08:53.491 --> 08:56.619
They say the Empress Dowager
established it.

08:56.702 --> 08:57.787
The Empress Dowager?

08:58.496 --> 09:01.207
It was during a time when
the Empress Regnant's power was strong,

09:01.290 --> 09:03.417
so it seems she couldn’t
set it up officially.

09:04.669 --> 09:05.503
I see.

09:06.504 --> 09:10.049
The Empress Dowager is kind, isn’t she?

09:12.885 --> 09:16.722
Plus, the ban on eunuchs and slavery...

09:16.806 --> 09:19.350
I heard that was due to
her influence as well.

09:21.269 --> 09:23.396
<i>From a humanity perspective,</i>

09:23.479 --> 09:25.731
<i>abolishing slavery is a good thing.</i>

09:25.815 --> 09:29.860
<i>But putting aside
those treated like livestock,</i>

09:29.944 --> 09:33.864
<i>cases where maids use themselves
as collateral for debt</i>

09:33.948 --> 09:36.701
<i>are considered legally similar
to employment.</i>

09:37.201 --> 09:39.245
<i>Still, from an outsider’s view,</i>

09:39.328 --> 09:41.831
<i>there’s little difference between
a maid and a slave.</i>

09:42.331 --> 09:46.794
<i>Granny said she was really nervous
when the abolition was decided.</i>

09:46.877 --> 09:49.672
<i>Officially, slavery has been abolished,</i>

09:49.755 --> 09:53.676
<i>but it’s common knowledge that
it still exists under a different name.</i>

09:54.719 --> 09:57.346
Well then, I should be heading back soon.

09:58.055 --> 10:01.142
Maomao, if you keep wandering around
too much, won’t you get scolded?

10:02.226 --> 10:03.811
Yeah, but...

10:04.812 --> 10:07.690
<i>The Empress Dowager
is heading to the clinic.</i>

10:07.773 --> 10:09.108
<i>Could it be related to</i>

10:09.191 --> 10:11.819
<i>the Crystal Pavilion incident
from the other day?</i>

10:12.653 --> 10:14.697
<i>If the Empress Dowager
is getting involved,</i>

10:14.780 --> 10:18.492
<i>there might be reform
in the palace’s medical system.</i>

10:18.576 --> 10:21.454
<i>I’d love to hear more about that, but...</i>

10:24.540 --> 10:26.417
- Yeah, I’d better go home.
- Huh?

10:27.209 --> 10:29.795
<i>I’ve been making people mad lately...</i>

10:30.504 --> 10:31.547
Do it again!

10:31.631 --> 10:32.798
Yes...

10:34.175 --> 10:35.259
<i>This is the third time.</i>

10:35.926 --> 10:39.138
<i>I was starting to think she finally
started picking on me...</i>

10:39.722 --> 10:41.515
- Clean more thoroughly!
- Yes!

10:41.599 --> 10:43.267
- There!
- Yes!

10:43.351 --> 10:45.645
<i>The other attendants
are getting criticized too.</i>

10:45.728 --> 10:49.440
Clean more thoroughly than usual!
Not a speck of dust should be left behind.

10:49.523 --> 10:52.902
<i>Huh? Is someone coming?</i>

10:55.863 --> 10:58.616
It’s been a while, Lady Anshi.

11:02.161 --> 11:04.413
<i>It’s the Empress Dowager!</i>

11:05.498 --> 11:07.333
Have you been well?

11:08.042 --> 11:09.960
Thank you for your concern.

11:10.544 --> 11:14.215
<i>Does the Empress Dowager know about
Lady Gyokuyou's pregnancy?</i>

11:14.882 --> 11:17.718
<i>So that must mean
that she’s really trusted.</i>

11:22.515 --> 11:24.683
<i>Rather than a mother-in-law
and daughter-in-law,</i>

11:24.767 --> 11:28.145
<i>they are more like friends
with a bit of an age gap.</i>

11:28.979 --> 11:30.147
You...

11:31.357 --> 11:34.568
You’re the attendant Jinshi assigned,
aren’t you?

11:34.652 --> 11:36.904
Yes, that’s right.

11:36.987 --> 11:38.072
<i>How does she know that?</i>

11:38.739 --> 11:40.658
Suiren told me.

11:40.741 --> 11:44.161
She said a girl worth training
has returned to the rear palace.

11:44.245 --> 11:47.415
Suiren used to be my attendant
a long time ago.

11:49.375 --> 11:50.626
I see.

11:50.709 --> 11:52.920
<i>So that sly attendant
and the Empress Dowager</i>

11:53.003 --> 11:55.089
<i>were old acquaintances.</i>

12:00.428 --> 12:01.637
Lady Anshi,

12:01.720 --> 12:05.558
pardon me, but Lingli seems tired.

12:05.641 --> 12:07.726
May I put her to bed?

12:08.477 --> 12:10.521
Yes. Go ahead.

12:14.775 --> 12:16.402
She's quite perceptive.

12:17.069 --> 12:18.279
She really is.

12:20.281 --> 12:22.700
Now, have a seat over here.

12:23.284 --> 12:24.452
Yes.

12:25.995 --> 12:27.204
You know,

12:27.288 --> 12:30.541
I hear you’ve been solving
all sorts of problems.

12:32.877 --> 12:36.213
I’m just applying the knowledge I have

12:36.297 --> 12:39.216
to situations where it fits.

12:42.052 --> 12:44.430
<i>Did that sound negative?</i>

12:44.513 --> 12:45.764
<i>But really,</i>

12:45.848 --> 12:47.892
<i>I don’t have a wild imagination,</i>

12:47.975 --> 12:49.894
<i>nor do I have my father’s vast knowledge.</i>

12:50.978 --> 12:53.772
<i>I can’t stay calm
unless I tell them upfront.</i>

12:54.398 --> 12:57.401
<i>That’s just my principle. I can’t help it.</i>

13:01.697 --> 13:03.240
That’s fine.

13:07.161 --> 13:08.996
Just tell me what you can understand.

13:10.164 --> 13:12.041
I want you to investigate something.

13:16.086 --> 13:17.296
Did I...

13:20.132 --> 13:23.344
place a curse on the late Emperor?

13:41.362 --> 13:43.113
A curse, huh?

13:43.656 --> 13:46.951
<i>It’s not unreasonable to think that way.</i>

13:47.993 --> 13:49.578
<i>To be honest, I’ve never heard</i>

13:49.662 --> 13:52.665
<i>anything good about the previous Emperor.</i>

13:52.748 --> 13:56.627
<i>A foolish brother, a dim-witted lord,
a puppet of the Empress Regnant.</i>

13:56.710 --> 13:59.296
<i>But the most well-known thing
about him in the rear palace</i>

13:59.380 --> 14:00.965
<i>was that he was attracted to young girls.</i>

14:02.925 --> 14:05.010
<i>Political marriages and settling debts</i>

14:05.094 --> 14:07.221
<i>by taking young brides does happen.</i>

14:07.805 --> 14:09.848
<i>However, even though
there were plenty of women</i>

14:09.932 --> 14:12.017
<i>of appropriate age in the selection,</i>

14:12.101 --> 14:14.728
<i>he always chose the youngest girls.</i>

14:16.438 --> 14:18.774
<i>The Empress Dowager bears
a scar on her stomach.</i>

14:19.900 --> 14:22.278
<i>When she gave birth
to the current Emperor,</i>

14:22.361 --> 14:25.781
<i>her body was still not fully developed,</i>

14:25.865 --> 14:27.992
<i>so she had no choice but
to have her stomach cut open.</i>

14:28.576 --> 14:31.495
<i>And the one who was
forcibly made into a eunuch</i>

14:31.579 --> 14:33.581
<i>just to assist in that childbirth</i>

14:33.664 --> 14:36.250
<i>was my unfortunate father, Luomen.</i>

14:36.959 --> 14:39.044
<i>Perhaps because of such sacrifices,</i>

14:39.128 --> 14:41.255
<i>the current Emperor grew up healthy,</i>

14:41.338 --> 14:44.758
<i>and the Empress Dowager later
gave birth to imperial younger brother.</i>

14:45.342 --> 14:47.219
<i>If I remember correctly,
the imperial younger brother</i>

14:47.303 --> 14:49.138
<i>is one year older than me.</i>

14:49.638 --> 14:52.766
<i>When the Empress Dowager gave birth,
she was nearly 30.</i>

14:53.642 --> 14:55.769
<i>She was far from being
considered a young girl.</i>

14:56.478 --> 14:58.022
<i>If that’s the case...</i>

14:59.231 --> 15:03.027
<i>Is the prince really
the former Emperor’s child?</i>

15:04.111 --> 15:07.740
<i>If I were to say something like this
aloud, I’d probably be beheaded.</i>

15:11.535 --> 15:13.746
<i>A few days later, the Empress Dowager</i>

15:13.829 --> 15:15.247
<i>arranged a tea party,</i>

15:15.331 --> 15:18.250
<i>bringing together
the four high-ranking consorts.</i>

15:18.834 --> 15:20.753
Lady Gyokuyou, this way.

15:20.836 --> 15:23.505
There’s still some time
before the tea party begins,

15:23.589 --> 15:25.341
so please take some rest.

15:25.424 --> 15:27.509
Yes, I’ll do that.

15:30.804 --> 15:32.598
<i>Lady Gyokuyou is still experiencing</i>

15:32.681 --> 15:35.517
<i>the drowsiness typical of early pregnancy.</i>

15:36.894 --> 15:39.438
What is the Empress Dowager planning?

15:39.521 --> 15:41.815
A tea party outside the rear palace?

15:41.899 --> 15:44.610
Even if it’s outside,
it’s still within the inner court.

15:44.693 --> 15:46.362
Plus, it’s His Majesty’s residence.

15:46.445 --> 15:49.114
That makes it even more nerve-wracking!

15:49.198 --> 15:51.075
It’s not a place we usually enter.

15:51.158 --> 15:53.035
The Empress Dowager is aware

15:53.118 --> 15:55.120
that Lady Gyokuyou is pregnant,

15:55.204 --> 15:56.288
so why do this now?

15:56.372 --> 15:58.332
That’s true,

15:58.415 --> 16:01.001
I’m sure she’ll take
that into consideration, but...

16:01.085 --> 16:03.337
When it comes to the other consorts,

16:03.420 --> 16:06.382
who knows what they might do?

16:07.383 --> 16:10.678
<i>Lady Gyokuyou's pregnancy
is an open secret,</i>

16:10.761 --> 16:13.055
<i>but in a face-to-face tea gathering,</i>

16:13.138 --> 16:15.891
<i>they might openly
try to probe for information.</i>

16:16.892 --> 16:18.477
<i>However, Lady Lihua</i>

16:18.560 --> 16:21.897
<i>wouldn't ask any questions
that might implicate herself.</i>

16:22.690 --> 16:25.859
<i>Besides, Lady Lihua, who has
always been proud and dignified,</i>

16:25.943 --> 16:28.696
<i>would never try to disgrace someone else.</i>

16:28.779 --> 16:30.447
<i>For Lady Gyokuyou as well,</i>

16:30.531 --> 16:33.200
<i>it wouldn't be wise
to quarrel with Lady Lihua,</i>

16:33.283 --> 16:34.910
<i>whose lineage is even more noble.</i>

16:35.494 --> 16:37.287
<i>If anyone were to say something,</i>

16:37.371 --> 16:39.623
<i>it would likely be Lady Lishu
who was tricked by her attendant.</i>

16:39.707 --> 16:43.419
<i>But I don't think the head attendant,
a former poisoner, would do that.</i>

16:44.753 --> 16:46.714
<i>If anything, the one to watch out for
is Lady Loulan.</i>

16:47.506 --> 16:49.550
<i>Apart from her flashy attire,</i>

16:49.633 --> 16:51.885
<i>there’s strangely little gossip about her.</i>

16:54.263 --> 16:57.016
Maomao, do you have a moment?

16:58.726 --> 16:59.727
Yes.

17:03.856 --> 17:05.190
What is it?

17:05.274 --> 17:07.818
I’ll be the one tasting for poison today.

17:07.901 --> 17:10.821
You understand what that means, right?

17:11.488 --> 17:12.322
I understand.

17:13.907 --> 17:17.745
<i>For the Empress Dowager to host
a gathering without assigning</i>

17:17.828 --> 17:18.829
<i>a poison taster implies that</i>

17:18.912 --> 17:21.832
<i>she trusts the attendees.</i>

17:22.416 --> 17:24.043
And as for you,

17:25.002 --> 17:27.921
the Empress Dowager
has requested your assistance.

17:29.256 --> 17:31.842
Has another problem been brought to you?

17:33.427 --> 17:38.098
Did I place a curse on the late Emperor?

17:38.182 --> 17:39.808
<i>If possible,</i>

17:39.892 --> 17:42.186
<i>I’d prefer to have this conversation
somewhere else.</i>

17:42.770 --> 17:46.273
It doesn't matter.
I'm sure you can't tell me anyway.

17:46.356 --> 17:47.316
However!

17:47.941 --> 17:51.653
Make sure you don't do anything
to betray Lady Gyokuyou.

17:53.489 --> 17:56.992
I have no intention of making
you an enemy, Lady Hongniang.

18:00.913 --> 18:02.664
Good.

18:02.748 --> 18:05.375
I'd like to maintain a good relationship
with you too, Maomao.

18:06.585 --> 18:07.836
That's true...

18:08.545 --> 18:09.880
<i>Lady Hongniang is</i>

18:09.963 --> 18:13.425
<i>undoubtedly suited to being
Lady Gyokuyou’s head attendant.</i>

18:18.347 --> 18:21.892
<i>If the Empress Dowager is calling for me,
it must be about that curse.</i>

18:26.271 --> 18:27.523
Sorry to keep you waiting.

18:28.190 --> 18:29.525
This way.

18:31.193 --> 18:33.320
Before the current rear palace was built,

18:33.403 --> 18:35.864
this place used to
serve as the rear palace.

18:36.448 --> 18:37.825
Is that so?

18:39.368 --> 18:41.495
<i>There’s no sign of people here,</i>

18:41.578 --> 18:44.039
<i>yet it's spotless,
without even a speck of dust.</i>

18:50.295 --> 18:54.049
<i>Even the raked gravel of
the dry landscape garden is clean.</i>

18:57.094 --> 18:58.053
This is the place.

18:59.429 --> 19:01.140
You may not go any further.

19:01.223 --> 19:02.891
Even the cleaning staff

19:02.975 --> 19:05.269
are not permitted beyond this point.

19:14.486 --> 19:15.946
<i>What is this smell?</i>

19:17.030 --> 19:17.865
<i>This room is...?</i>

19:20.242 --> 19:22.452
During the reign of
the emperor before last,

19:22.536 --> 19:23.620
an attendant,

19:23.704 --> 19:26.957
who became a consort
of lower rank, lived here.

19:28.500 --> 19:31.211
This was the room of the woman
known as the Late Empress Regnant,

19:31.295 --> 19:34.089
the place where
the late emperor was raised,

19:34.173 --> 19:35.841
and also where she passed away.

19:40.012 --> 19:41.221
Let’s move to another location.

19:55.360 --> 19:57.654
In his later years, the late emperor

19:57.738 --> 19:59.907
and his mother,
who was called the late Empress Regnant,

19:59.990 --> 20:02.659
began spending more and more time
secluded in that room.

20:04.077 --> 20:06.580
<i>As if clinging to memories,
he immersed himself there.</i>

20:06.663 --> 20:08.832
<i>Perhaps the late emperor
had grown weak in spirit,</i>

20:09.416 --> 20:11.001
<i>because after the Empress Regnant
passed away,</i>

20:11.084 --> 20:14.338
<i>he followed shortly after,
drawing his last breath in that room.</i>

20:14.922 --> 20:18.884
Forgive me for asking,
but he wasn’t particularly young, was he?

20:18.967 --> 20:22.095
He had lived a full life, so you
could say he passed away at an old age.

20:22.179 --> 20:25.182
Then why does the Empress Dowager
believe it was a curse?

20:26.433 --> 20:27.976
I, too, told her that there was

20:28.060 --> 20:29.853
no such thing as a curse.

20:29.937 --> 20:31.688
However, Lady Anshi said...

20:32.272 --> 20:35.692
I cursed him. I wished he would disappear.

20:36.985 --> 20:38.362
Night after night...

20:39.488 --> 20:41.740
For so, so long... I kept thinking about it.

20:43.867 --> 20:45.077
Is there

20:45.160 --> 20:47.955
any actual proof
that a curse was involved?

20:50.540 --> 20:53.210
The late emperor’s body

20:53.293 --> 20:55.712
was enshrined in the mausoleum for a year.

20:56.421 --> 20:59.049
<i>The following year,
His Majesty and Lady Anshi viewed</i>

20:59.132 --> 21:00.717
<i>the late emperor’s remains
before the burial.</i>

21:00.801 --> 21:03.428
<i>And when they saw his body...</i>

21:05.305 --> 21:06.640
<i>it had remained</i>

21:06.723 --> 21:10.310
<i>almost exactly the same
as when he had passed.</i>

21:12.688 --> 21:15.107
In other words, it hadn't decayed?

21:15.691 --> 21:19.027
Yes. The Empress Regnant, who passed away
around the same time...

21:19.111 --> 21:22.406
Let's just say her remains were
in a state too horrific to describe.

21:23.699 --> 21:25.284
And so, Lady Anshi

21:25.367 --> 21:27.661
believes she herself placed
a curse on the late emperor.

21:27.744 --> 21:28.870
Yes.

21:29.788 --> 21:31.665
<i>I see.</i>

21:32.541 --> 21:34.710
<i>The mausoleum stays cool even in summer,</i>

21:34.793 --> 21:37.170
<i>but unless a body is preserved in ice,</i>

21:37.754 --> 21:40.632
<i>it will naturally decay, attract insects,
and dry up over time.</i>

21:41.425 --> 21:44.678
<i>The fact that this didn’t happen
is certainly unusual.</i>

21:45.345 --> 21:47.848
<i>All humans return to the earth.</i>

21:47.931 --> 21:50.600
<i>Whether an aristocrat or a farmer,
it is the same.</i>

21:50.684 --> 21:53.020
<i>No matter our social standing at birth,</i>

21:53.103 --> 21:55.188
<i>this one fate is shared by all.</i>

21:56.023 --> 21:59.359
That wing of the palace is
set to be demolished soon.

21:59.443 --> 22:01.653
Before that happens,
I would like you to investigate it.

22:01.737 --> 22:03.280
Understood.

22:03.780 --> 22:06.908
But I have one request.

22:08.201 --> 22:09.494
A request?

23:46.049 --> 23:49.678
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

23:57.269 --> 24:00.063
<i>The next episode is "The Late Emperor."</i>

24:00.147 --> 24:01.857
Subtitle translation by:
Abhishek Chand Ramola
